    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "When {@link CharRange#isIn(char, char)} is given endpoints in descending order ('Z' before 'W'), the constructor swaps them so the range always runs from the lower character to the higher one. The resulting range is therefore a normal (non-negated) range whose start is 'W' and end is 'Z'. <p>Iterating the range via {@link CharRange#forEach} should complete without error, here exercised with a mock {@link Consumer}.</p>"
